# =============================================================================
# Lv-00 Axiom Package: Quantum Information Theory
# =============================================================================
#
# Mathematical Theory: Quantum Information Theory — the mathematical study
# of information encoding, transmission, and processing using quantum
# mechanical systems. Combines quantum mechanics with information theory,
# providing the foundation for quantum computing, quantum cryptography,
# and quantum communication.
#
# References:
#   - Nielsen, M.A. & Chuang, I.L. (2010). "Quantum Computation and Quantum
#     Information" (10th Anniversary Edition). Cambridge University Press.
#     ISBN 978-1-107-00217-3. https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511976667
#   - Wilde, M.M. (2017). "Quantum Information Theory" (2nd ed.).
#     Cambridge University Press. ISBN 978-1-316-80994-8.
#   - Preskill, J. (1998). "Quantum Information and Computation."
#     Lecture Notes, Caltech. http://theory.caltech.edu/~preskill/ph219/
#   - Watrous, J. (2018). "The Theory of Quantum Information."
#     Cambridge University Press. ISBN 978-1-107-18056-7.
#   - Bengtsson, I. & Życzkowski, K. (2017). "Geometry of Quantum States"
#     (2nd ed.). Cambridge University Press. ISBN 978-1-107-02256-4.
#   - Holevo, A.S. (2019). "Quantum Systems, Channels, Information" (2nd ed.).
#     De Gruyter. ISBN 978-3-11-064224-9.
#   - Hayashi, M. (2006). "Quantum Information Theory: Mathematical Foundation."
#     Springer. ISBN 978-3-662-49624-6.
#   - Wikipedia: Quantum information
#     https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_information
#   - Wikipedia: Quantum channel
#     https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_channel
#   - Wikipedia: Quantum entanglement
#     https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_entanglement
#   - Wikipedia: Qubit
#     https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qubit
#   - Wikipedia: Density matrix
#     https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Density_matrix
#   - Wikipedia: Von Neumann entropy
#     https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Von_Neumann_entropy
#   - Wikipedia: Quantum teleportation
#     https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_teleportation
#   - Wikipedia: No-cloning theorem
#     https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No-cloning_theorem
#   - Wikipedia: Quantum error correction
#     https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_error_correction
#   - nLab: quantum information
#     https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/quantum+information
#   - nLab: quantum channel
#     https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/quantum+channel
#
# Primitive Notions:
#   - Hilbert space H (state space of quantum system)
#   - Quantum state ρ (density operator: positive semidefinite, trace 1)
#   - Pure state |ψ⟩ (rank-1 density operator)
#   - Qubit (2-dimensional quantum system)
#   - Quantum channel Φ (CPTP map: completely positive, trace-preserving)
#   - Observable A (Hermitian operator)
#   - Measurement {M_i} (POVM: positive operators summing to identity)
#   - Entanglement (non-separable bipartite state)
#
# Core Axioms (Quantum Postulates):
#
#   QP1. State Space Postulate:
#       A quantum system is associated with a Hilbert space H.
#       The state of the system is described by a density operator ρ
#       satisfying: ρ ≥ 0 (positive semidefinite), Tr(ρ) = 1.
#
#   QP2. Evolution Postulate:
#       The evolution of a closed quantum system is described by a
#       unitary transformation: ρ → UρU†, where U is unitary (U†U = I).
#       Open system evolution is a CPTP map (quantum channel).
#
#   QP3. Measurement Postulate:
#       A measurement is described by a POVM {M_i} with M_i ≥ 0, Σ_i M_i = I.
#       Probability of outcome i: p_i = Tr(M_i ρ).
#       Post-measurement state (if outcome i): ρ_i = √M_i ρ √M_i / p_i.
#
#   QP4. Composite System Postulate:
#       The state space of a composite system is the tensor product of
#       component state spaces: H_AB = H_A ⊗ H_B.
#       The state of a composite system may be entangled (non-separable).
#
# Key Derived Concepts:
#   - Qubit: |ψ⟩ = α|0⟩ + β|1⟩ with |α|² + |β|² = 1
#   - Bloch sphere representation of single-qubit states
#   - Schmidt decomposition for bipartite pure states
#   - Von Neumann entropy: S(ρ) = -Tr(ρ log ρ)
#   - Quantum mutual information: I(A;B) = S(ρ_A) + S(ρ_B) - S(ρ_AB)
#   - Entanglement entropy (for pure states)
#   - Concurrence and entanglement of formation
#   - Quantum channel capacities (classical, quantum, private)
#   - Holevo bound: classical information from quantum systems
#   - No-cloning theorem: unknown quantum states cannot be perfectly copied
#   - Quantum teleportation: transferring quantum states using entanglement
#   - Quantum key distribution (BB84, E91 protocols)
#   - Quantum error correction codes
#   - Bell inequalities and nonlocality
#
# Known Undecidable / Unconstructible Problems:
#   - Quantum separability problem: determining if a state is separable
#     (NP-hard in general)
#   - Quantum channel capacity computation (no closed-form formula)
#   - Optimal quantum measurement discrimination
#   - Quantum state discrimination (optimal strategy may not exist)
#   - Decidability of quantum entanglement detection
#   - Quantum complexity class relationships (BQP vs NP is open)
#   - Quantum circuit optimization (finding minimal circuit is hard)
#   - Quantum error correction code optimization
#
# Relationship to Other Lv-00 Axiom Packages:
#   - information_theory: Quantum entropy generalizes Shannon entropy;
#     Holevo bound limits classical information from quantum systems
#   - functional_analysis: Hilbert spaces are central; density operators
#     are trace-class operators; quantum channels are CPTP maps
#   - probability_theory: Quantum states are probability measures on
#     the space of pure states; measurement outcomes are probabilistic
#   - linear_algebra (implied): Matrix operations, tensor products,
#     spectral decomposition, unitary matrices
#   - group_theory: Pauli matrices form a group; unitary representations
#   - category_theory: Quantum channels form a category; C*-algebras
#   - computability_theory: Quantum computing extends classical computing
#
# Author: Lv-00 Axiom Package System (AI-Discovered)
# Date: 2026-05-24
# Version: 1.0.0
# =============================================================================

axiom "quantum_information_theory" "1.0.0" {

    # =================================================================
    # Group I: Quantum Postulates (4)
    # =================================================================

    # QP1. State Space Postulate: Quantum states are density operators
    # A density operator ρ satisfies: ρ ≥ 0 (positive semidefinite), Tr(ρ) = 1
    template "quantum_state_density_operator" 1

    # QP2. Unitary Evolution: Closed system evolution is unitary
    # ρ → UρU† where U†U = I
    template "unitary_evolution" 2

    # QP3. Measurement Postulate: POVM measurement
    # {M_i} with M_i ≥ 0, Σ_i M_i = I; p_i = Tr(M_i ρ)
    template "povm_measurement" 2

    # QP4. Composite System: Tensor product structure
    # H_AB = H_A ⊗ H_B
    template "composite_system_tensor_product" 2

    # =================================================================
    # Group II: Qubit and Single-Qubit States (10)
    # =================================================================

    # QUB1. Qubit definition: 2-dimensional quantum system
    template "qubit_definition" 0

    # QUB2. Qubit pure state: |ψ⟩ = α|0⟩ + β|1⟩ with |α|² + |β|² = 1
    template "qubit_pure_state" 2

    # QUB3. Bloch sphere representation:
    # ρ = (I + r⃗·σ⃗)/2 where |r⃗| ≤ 1
    template "bloch_sphere_representation" 1

    # QUB4. Pauli matrices: σ_x, σ_y, σ_z
    template "pauli_matrices" 0

    # QUB5. Computational basis: |0⟩, |1⟩
    template "computational_basis" 0

    # QUB6. Hadamard basis: |+⟩, |−⟩
    template "hadamard_basis" 0

    # QUB7. Qubit density matrix: 2×2 positive semidefinite, trace 1
    template "qubit_density_matrix" 1

    # QUB8. Single-qubit unitary gates: I, X, Y, Z, H, S, T
    template "single_qubit_gates" 1

    # QUB9. Bloch vector: r⃗ = (Tr(ρX), Tr(ρY), Tr(ρZ))
    template "bloch_vector" 1

    # QUB10. Pure state condition: Tr(ρ²) = 1
    template "pure_state_condition" 1

    # =================================================================
    # Group III: Quantum States and Density Operators (12)
    # =================================================================

    # QS1. Density operator properties: ρ ≥ 0, Tr(ρ) = 1
    template "density_operator_properties" 1

    # QS2. Pure state: rank-1 projector |ψ⟩⟨ψ|
    template "pure_state_projector" 1

    # QS3. Mixed state: convex combination of pure states
    template "mixed_state_convex_combination" 1

    # QS4. Spectral decomposition: ρ = Σ_i λ_i |i⟩⟨i|
    template "spectral_decomposition" 1

    # QS5. Partial trace: Tr_B(ρ_AB) = ρ_A
    template "partial_trace" 2

    # QS6. State purification: Every mixed state has a purification
    template "state_purification" 1

    # QS7. Schmidt decomposition: |ψ⟩_AB = Σ_i √λ_i |i⟩_A ⊗ |i⟩_B
    template "schmidt_decomposition" 1

    # QS8. Schmidt rank: number of non-zero Schmidt coefficients
    template "schmidt_rank" 1

    # QS9. Fidelity: F(ρ, σ) = Tr(√(√ρ σ √ρ))
    template "fidelity_definition" 2

    # QS10. Trace distance: D(ρ, σ) = (1/2)||ρ - σ||_1
    template "trace_distance" 2

    # QS11. Ensemble representation: ρ = Σ_i p_i |ψ_i⟩⟨ψ_i|
    template "ensemble_representation" 2

    # QS12. State discrimination: optimal measurement to distinguish states
    template "state_discrimination" 2

    # =================================================================
    # Group IV: Quantum Channels (CPTP Maps) (12)
    # =================================================================

    # QC1. Quantum channel definition: CPTP map Φ
    template "quantum_channel_cptp" 1

    # QC2. Complete positivity: (I ⊗ Φ)(ρ) ≥ 0 for all ρ ≥ 0
    template "complete_positivity" 1

    # QC3. Trace preservation: Tr(Φ(ρ)) = Tr(ρ)
    template "trace_preservation" 1

    # QC4. Kraus representation: Φ(ρ) = Σ_i K_i ρ K_i† with Σ_i K_i†K_i = I
    template "kraus_representation" 2

    # QC5. Stinespring dilation: Every channel has a unitary extension
    template "stinespring_dilation" 1

    # QC6. Choi matrix: J_Φ = (I ⊗ Φ)(|Ω⟩⟨Ω|) where |Ω⟩ = Σ_i |i⟩⊗|i⟩
    template "choi_matrix" 1

    # QC7. Unitary channel: Φ(ρ) = UρU†
    template "unitary_channel" 2

    # QC8. Depolarizing channel: Φ(ρ) = (1-p)ρ + p(I/d)
    template "depolarizing_channel" 2

    # QC9. Amplitude damping channel: models energy dissipation
    template "amplitude_damping_channel" 2

    # QC10. Phase damping channel: models dephasing
    template "phase_damping_channel" 2

    # QC11. Bit flip channel: X error with probability p
    template "bit_flip_channel" 2

    # QC12. Phase flip channel: Z error with probability p
    template "phase_flip_channel" 2

    # =================================================================
    # Group V: Quantum Entanglement (12)
    # =================================================================

    # QE1. Separable state: ρ_AB = Σ_i p_i ρ_A^i ⊗ ρ_B^i
    template "separable_state" 1

    # QE2. Entangled state: not separable
    template "entangled_state" 1

    # QE3. Bell states: maximally entangled two-qubit states
    template "bell_states" 0

    # QE4. Maximally entangled state: |Φ⁺⟩ = (|00⟩ + |11⟩)/√2
    template "maximally_entangled_state" 0

    # QE5. Entanglement entropy: S(ρ_A) for pure |ψ⟩_AB
    template "entanglement_entropy" 1

    # QE6. Concurrence: entanglement measure for two qubits
    template "concurrence" 1

    # QE7. Entanglement of formation: E_F(ρ) = min{Σ_i p_i S(Tr_B|ψ_i⟩⟨ψ_i|)}
    template "entanglement_of_formation" 1

    # QE8. PPT criterion (Peres-Horodecki): separable ⟹ PPT
    template "ppt_criterion" 1

    # QE9. Partial transpose: ρ^(T_B) for entanglement detection
    template "partial_transpose" 1

    # QE10. Entanglement witness: W such that Tr(Wρ) < 0 iff ρ entangled
    template "entanglement_witness" 2

    # QE11. LOCC (Local Operations and Classical Communication)
    template "locc_operations" 0

    # QE12. Distillable entanglement: maximum entanglement extractable via LOCC
    template "distillable_entanglement" 1

    # =================================================================
    # Group VI: Quantum Entropy and Information (10)
    # =================================================================

    # QI1. Von Neumann entropy: S(ρ) = -Tr(ρ log ρ)
    template "von_neumann_entropy" 1

    # QI2. Quantum relative entropy: D(ρ||σ) = Tr(ρ(log ρ - log σ))
    template "quantum_relative_entropy" 2

    # QI3. Quantum mutual information: I(A;B) = S(ρ_A) + S(ρ_B) - S(ρ_AB)
    template "quantum_mutual_information" 1

    # QI4. Conditional entropy: S(A|B) = S(ρ_AB) - S(ρ_B)
    template "quantum_conditional_entropy" 1

    # QI5. Strong subadditivity: S(ρ_ABC) + S(ρ_B) ≤ S(ρ_AB) + S(ρ_BC)
    template "strong_subadditivity" 1

    # QI6. Araki-Lieb inequality: |S(ρ_A) - S(ρ_B)| ≤ S(ρ_AB)
    template "araki_lieb_inequality" 1

    # QI7. Holevo bound: χ ≤ S(ρ) - Σ_i p_i S(ρ_i)
    template "holevo_bound" 2

    # QI8. Quantum data processing inequality
    template "quantum_data_processing" 2

    # QI9. Quantum channel capacity: maximum rate of reliable transmission
    template "quantum_channel_capacity" 1

    # QI10. Coherent information: I_c(ρ, Φ) = S(Φ(ρ)) - S((I ⊗ Φ)(|ψ⟩⟨ψ|))
    template "coherent_information" 2

    # =================================================================
    # Group VII: Quantum Measurements (8)
    # =================================================================

    # QM1. Projective measurement: {P_i} with P_i² = P_i, P_i P_j = δ_{ij} P_i
    template "projective_measurement" 1

    # QM2. POVM (Positive Operator-Valued Measure): {M_i} with M_i ≥ 0
    template "povm_definition" 1

    # QM3. Naimark dilation: POVM extends to projective measurement
    template "naimark_dilation" 1

    # QM4. Measurement in computational basis
    template "computational_basis_measurement" 1

    # QM5. Bell measurement: measurement in Bell basis
    template "bell_measurement" 1

    # QM6. Weak measurement: minimal disturbance measurement
    template "weak_measurement" 2

    # QM7. POVM optimization: optimal measurement for state discrimination
    template "povm_optimization" 2

    # QM8. Measurement disturbance: how measurement affects the state
    template "measurement_disturbance" 2

    # =================================================================
    # Group VIII: Fundamental Theorems (8)
    # =================================================================

    # FT1. No-cloning theorem: unknown quantum states cannot be copied
    template "no_cloning_theorem" 0

    # FT2. No-broadcast theorem: quantum information cannot be broadcast
    template "no_broadcast_theorem" 0

    # FT3. No-deleting theorem: unknown quantum states cannot be deleted
    template "no_deleting_theorem" 0

    # FT4. No-hiding theorem: quantum information is conserved
    template "no_hiding_theorem" 0

    # FT5. No-teleportation theorem: cannot determine unknown quantum state
    template "no_teleportation_theorem" 0

    # FT6. Quantum teleportation: transfer quantum state using entanglement
    template "quantum_teleportation" 0

    # FT7. Superdense coding: send 2 classical bits with 1 qubit
    template "superdense_coding" 0

    # FT8. Holevo's theorem: bound on classical information from quantum
    template "holevo_theorem" 0

    # =================================================================
    # Group IX: Quantum Gates and Circuits (10)
    # =================================================================

    # QG1. Single-qubit gates: rotations on Bloch sphere
    template "single_qubit_gate" 2

    # QG2. Two-qubit gates: CNOT, CZ, SWAP
    template "two_qubit_gates" 0

    # QG3. CNOT gate: controlled-NOT
    template "cnot_gate" 0

    # QG4. Universal gate set: {H, T, CNOT} is universal
    template "universal_gate_set" 0

    # QG5. Quantum circuit: sequence of quantum gates
    template "quantum_circuit" 1

    # QG6. Clifford gates: H, S, CNOT
    template "clifford_gates" 0

    # QG7. Non-Clifford gate: T gate (π/8 gate)
    template "non_clifford_gate" 0

    # QG8. Gate decomposition: any unitary as circuit
    template "gate_decomposition" 1

    # QG9. Circuit depth and width
    template "circuit_complexity" 2

    # QG10. Solovay-Kitaev theorem: efficient gate approximation
    template "solovay_kitaev_theorem" 0

    # =================================================================
    # Group X: Quantum Error Correction (8)
    # =================================================================

    # QEC1. Quantum error: Pauli errors X, Y, Z
    template "quantum_error_types" 0

    # QEC2. Error correction condition: [P_i, E_a] = 0 for stabilizer codes
    template "error_correction_condition" 2

    # QEC3. Stabilizer code: defined by stabilizer group
    template "stabilizer_code" 1

    # QEC4. Shor code: 9-qubit code correcting arbitrary single-qubit error
    template "shor_code" 0

    # QEC5. Steane code: 7-qubit CSS code
    template "steane_code" 0

    # QEC6. Surface code: topological quantum error correction
    template "surface_code" 0

    # QEC7. Quantum error detection: detect without correcting
    template "quantum_error_detection" 1

    # QEC8. Fault-tolerant computation: computation with error correction
    template "fault_tolerant_computation" 0

    # =================================================================
    # Group XI: Quantum Cryptography (6)
    # =================================================================

    # QCR1. BB84 protocol: quantum key distribution
    template "bb84_protocol" 0

    # QCR2. E91 protocol: entanglement-based QKD
    template "e91_protocol" 0

    # QCR3. Quantum secret sharing
    template "quantum_secret_sharing" 0

    # QCR4. Quantum digital signatures
    template "quantum_digital_signatures" 0

    # QCR5. Security proofs: unconditional security
    template "quantum_security_proofs" 0

    # QCR6. Eavesdropping detection: quantum advantage
    template "eavesdropping_detection" 0

    # =================================================================
    # Group XII: Bell Inequalities and Nonlocality (6)
    # =================================================================

    # BI1. Bell inequality: CHSH inequality |⟨CHSH⟩| ≤ 2 classically
    template "bell_inequality" 0

    # BI2. CHSH inequality: S = E(a,b) + E(a,b') + E(a',b) - E(a',b')
    template "chsh_inequality" 0

    # BI3. Bell state measurement: correlation measurements
    template "bell_state_measurement" 0

    # BI4. Tsirelson bound: quantum maximum |⟨CHSH⟩| ≤ 2√2
    template "tsirelson_bound" 0

    # BI5. Nonlocality: violation of Bell inequalities
    template "quantum_nonlocality" 0

    # BI6. Local hidden variable model: classical explanation
    template "local_hidden_variable" 0

    # =================================================================
    # Known Unconstructible / Undecidable Problems
    # =================================================================

    # UC1. Quantum separability problem
    # Determining if a given state is separable is NP-hard in general.
    unconstructible "quantum_separability_problem" {
        reduces_to "np_hard"
        dependency "computational_complexity_theory"
        external_ref "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_state_discrimination"
        green_verified true
    }

    # UC2. Quantum channel capacity computation
    # No closed-form formula exists for general quantum channel capacities.
    unconstructible "quantum_channel_capacity_computation" {
        reduces_to "optimization_problem"
        external_ref "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_channel_capacity"
        green_verified true
    }

    # UC3. Optimal quantum state discrimination
    # Finding optimal measurement to distinguish quantum states.
    unconstructible "optimal_state_discrimination" {
        reduces_to "optimization_problem"
        external_ref "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_state_discrimination"
        green_verified true
    }

    # UC4. BQP vs NP
    # Relationship between quantum and classical complexity classes is open.
    unconstructible "bqp_vs_np" {
        reduces_to "complexity_theory_open_problem"
        dependency "computational_complexity_theory"
        external_ref "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BQP"
        green_verified false
    }

    # UC5. Quantum circuit optimization
    # Finding minimal quantum circuit for a given unitary is hard.
    unconstructible "quantum_circuit_optimization" {
        reduces_to "optimization_problem"
        external_ref "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_circuit"
        green_verified true
    }

    # UC6. Entanglement detection for general states
    # No universal efficient criterion for entanglement detection.
    unconstructible "general_entanglement_detection" {
        reduces_to "quantum_separability_problem"
        external_ref "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_entanglement"
        green_verified true
    }

    # UC7. Quantum error correction code optimization
    # Finding optimal codes for given noise models.
    unconstructible "qec_code_optimization" {
        reduces_to "optimization_problem"
        external_ref "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_error_correction"
        green_verified true
    }

    # UC8. Quantum supremacy verification
    # Verifying quantum supremacy claims is computationally hard.
    unconstructible "quantum_supremacy_verification" {
        reduces_to "computational_complexity"
        dependency "computational_complexity_theory"
        external_ref "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_supremacy"
        green_verified true
    }

    # =================================================================
    # Logical Framework
    # =================================================================

    # Bottom geometry: Hilbert space with density operators
    # Quantum states are points in the space of density operators
    bottom_geometry "hilbert_space_density_operators"

    # Negation encoding: orthogonal complement in Hilbert space
    # ¬|ψ⟩ is represented by orthogonal state |ψ⊥⟩
    negation_encoding "hilbert_space_orthogonal_complement"

    # Contradiction behavior: explosion principle
    # Incompatible observables lead to uncertainty, not logical contradiction
    contradiction_behavior "explosion_principle"
}
